# Milestone: v0.10.11-channel-and-isA
# Covers: compound assignment operators (+=, *=, /=, -=) are evaluated atomically;
#         target expression is not evaluated twice even with side effects.
# blocked: T39 chk driver — interleaved output observation
# matrix-row: separator-pipe
#
# Reason:
#   cout/Channel I/O shipped at v0.10.11 (D6 full Channel).  Remaining
#   block is the T39 chk driver: the fixture interleaves `cout << "..."`
#   output with the expected-value lines `[NNNNNNNN] 2`, which requires
#   the T39 multi-line driver to align actual output against expected
#   tags across the boundary.  Class/prototype definition, slot-method
#   dispatch, and cout are all available post-v0.10.11; the test body
#   itself is ready to activate once the T39 driver lands.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when T39 chk driver lands):
# # cout.quote = false | class Base { function foo() { cout << "Hello world!"; return this }; var val = 0 };
# # Base.foo().val += 2;
# # [00000001:output] Hello world!
# # [00000002] 2
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/inplace-atomic.chk)
